    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find out how many students did not receive an A in either history or math, we can use the principle of inclusion and exclusion for counting.\n\nThe number of students who received an A in history is 7, and the number of students who received an A in math is 13. However, this counts the 4 students who received an A in both courses twice, once in the history count and once in the math count.\n\nSo, to find the total number of students who received at least one A, we add the numbers from both courses and then subtract the number of students who received A in both courses (to avoid double-counting).\n\nTotal students with an A = Students with A in history + Students with A in math - Students with A in both\n\nTotal students with an A = 7 + 13 - 4 = 26\n\nSince there are 30 students in total, the number of students who did not receive an A in any of these two courses is:\n\nTotal students - Students with an A = 30 - 26 = 4\n\nSo, 4 students did not receive an A in any of these two courses (history or math).",
